From 2cb2e6d3d4fd8a8e7f7c2c0f3f4d0b6f7a5b4c3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: boot-mode: match RK3588 SARADC by compatible

Mainline RK3588 device trees use the schema-compliant node name
adc@fec10000. The generic download-key check previously only accepted
device names beginning with saradc, so it skipped the real ADC device and
never sampled channel 1. Keep the legacy name fallback for older trees,
but match the RK3588 SARADC compatible as the stable identity.

Signed-off-by: BDY-G98 port <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -52,7 +52,8 @@ __weak int rockchip_dnl_key_pressed(void)
 	ret = -ENODEV;
 	uclass_foreach_dev(dev, uc) {
-		if (!strncmp(dev->name, "saradc", 6)) {
+		if (device_is_compatible(dev, "rockchip,rk3588-saradc") ||
+		    !strncmp(dev->name, "saradc", 6)) {
 			ret = adc_channel_single_shot(dev->name, 1, &val);
 			break;
		}
